{
  "schemaVersion": "atm.workItem.v0.2",
  "workItemId": "ATM-GOV-0348",
  "title": "Scope commit work admission to the ticket bundle, not the whole staged index",
  "status": "running",
  "milestone": null,
  "dependencies": [],
  "acceptance": [
    "ACC-1 A governed commit whose bundle lies wholly inside the ticket grant is admitted regardless of unrelated paths present in the shared index, with no flag required.",
    "ACC-2 Admission still denies when a path the commit would actually write is outside the grant. Scoping the selection must not become a way to smuggle an out-of-scope path past the gate.",
    "ACC-3 `--defer-foreign-staged` continues to control whether foreign staged entries are snapshotted and unstaged. It no longer controls whether admission is ticket-scoped, and it is no longer required to commit in-scope work.",
    "ACC-4 Foreign staged bytes are unchanged, byte for byte, across an admitted commit taken without any deferral flag."
  ],
  "deliverables": [
    "packages/cli/src/commands/git-governance.ts",
    "tests/cli/commit-admission-ticket-scoped-selection.test.ts"
  ],
  "scopePaths": [
